  <dialog id="mastery-dialog" class="wide-dialog" aria-labelledby="mastery-title"><button class="close icon-button" data-close aria-label="Close mastery and rewards">×</button><h2 id="mastery-title">Master the prism.</h2><p id="mastery-summary"></p><p>Earn Restored by clearing a world, Swift by beating its target, Flawless without losing a life, and Skilled through its special objective. Adventure, Daily and official Practice count. Edited workshop previews do not.</p><p id="mastery-save-status" class="small" role="status"></p><div id="mastery-grid" class="mastery-grid"></div><details id="collection-rewards"><summary>Rewards, exports &amp; play notes</summary><h3>Your rewards</h3><ul id="reward-list"></ul><p>Choose unlocked finishes and trails in Settings. Restore worlds to reveal their artwork and listen to their music below.</p><p id="collection-music-status" class="small" role="status"></p><div class="mastery-actions"><button id="export-mastery" class="button secondary">Export mastery</button><button id="import-mastery" class="button secondary">Import mastery</button><input id="import-mastery-file" type="file" accept="application/json,.json" hidden><button id="export-play-notes" class="button secondary">Export play notes</button></div></details></dialog>
- <dialog id="help-dialog" class="wide-dialog" aria-labelledby="help-title"><button class="close icon-button" data-close aria-label="Close"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/assets/icons.svg?v=4#x"/></svg></button><h2 id="help-title">One paddle. Your angle.</h2><p>Clear the bricks without losing all three lives. Hit with the paddle’s edges to steer the ball.</p><div class="control-guide"><div><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/assets/icons.svg?v=4#keyboard"/></svg><strong>Keyboard</strong><p><kbd>←</kbd> <kbd>→</kbd> or <kbd>A</kbd> <kbd>D</kbd> to move.<br><kbd>SPACE</kbd> to launch. <kbd>P</kbd> or <kbd>ESC</kbd> to pause.</p></div><div><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/assets/icons.svg?v=4#hand-finger"/></svg><strong>Mouse & touch</strong><p>Move the mouse or drag your finger to steer.<br>Click or tap the arena to launch.</p></div></div><section aria-labelledby="brick-guide-title"><h3 id="brick-guide-title">Know your bricks.</h3><div id="brick-guide" class="brick-guide"></div></section><h3>Master your next shot.</h3><p>Sticky catches keep the ball where it lands. With the new rules, a direction slider and guide let you aim before launching; Q and E also adjust aim. If three or fewer bricks remain and twelve active seconds pass without a break, you earn one Precision catch for that formation. Arm it below the arena, catch the next ball, aim and launch. It does not clear bricks automatically.</p><h3>Choose a strategy.</h3><p>Paired drops share one choice: collecting one removes its partner. Wide + Sticky forms a precision rig. Multiball + Pierce deals a second hit to surviving armor. Laser expands explosive chain reactions. Gold rings mark encounter generators; neutral rings mark protected cores and mint rings mark exposed cores. Read the encounter instructions below the arena. Storm cores announce their opening; Nexus uses switches and portals.</p><h3>Build your collection.</h3><p>Mastery &amp; rewards shows four independent medals per world, personal world records, earned cosmetics and restored artwork/music. Master this world starts official Practice with consistent challenge rules. Shared challenge links replay an official world and seed, with an optional target score and time. Practice remains outside the ranked boards. Moving barriers slow briefly during each authored recovery period; ball physics stay consistent. Old checkpoints retain their original rules.</p><h3>Take in the story.</h3><p>World endings and high-score scenes wait for you. Use the visible Continue action when you’re ready, or press Space or Enter while the story heading is focused. P or Escape pauses or resumes the animation and its music while the story heading is focused. Reduced motion is available in Settings.</p><h3>Catch a little advantage.</h3><div id="power-guide" class="power-guide"></div><section aria-labelledby="scoring-title"><h3 id="scoring-title">How scoring works.</h3><p>Destroying a brick earns <strong>100 × your combo multiplier</strong>. The combo counts bricks destroyed since the last paddle contact.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption class="sr-only">Points per brick within a combo streak</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">BRICKS IN STREAK</th><th scope="col">MULTIPLIER</th><th scope="col">POINTS EACH</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1–5</td><td>×1</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><td>6–11</td><td>×2</td><td>200</td></tr><tr><td>12–17</td><td>×3</td><td>300</td></tr><tr><td>18–23</td><td>×4</td><td>400</td></tr><tr><td>24 onward</td><td>×5</td><td>500</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>A 12-brick streak earns <strong>2,000 points</strong>. Any ball touching the paddle resets the shared combo, including a Sticky catch. Losing all balls or starting a new board also resets it. Laser shots and explosion chains build that same combo; armored bricks score only when destroyed.</p><p><strong>Clear bonus: 750 + 150 × lives remaining.</strong> Clear with three lives for 1,200 bonus points. The first two Citadel and Nexus formations award 500 each; the final formation uses the normal clear bonus. Earn an extra life every 12,000 points, up to nine lives.</p><p><strong>Every collected power-up earns 150 points.</strong> Pickup points are added directly, without a combo multiplier. Multiball, Laser and Piercing can build brick combos. Wide, Slow and Shield help preserve lives. Sticky helps you aim, but each catch resets the combo. Each Extra life retained at a normal clear adds 150 to its bonus.</p><p><strong>Speed bonus: up to 2,000 points for each board.</strong> Subtract 10 points for every whole active second: a 40-second clear earns 1,600; a 100-second clear earns 1,000; at 200 seconds the bonus reaches zero. Each Citadel and Nexus formation earns its own speed bonus. Leaderboards rank by score, then world reached, then shortest active play time. Pauses, cutscenes and waiting to launch after a life loss do not count toward time. Losing a life or saving and resuming does not reset the board timer.</p><p>Your personal best combines Adventure and Daily Challenge runs. Practice does not update it.</p></section><p class="small">Adventure follows all sixteen worlds. Practice lets you try any world. The daily challenge is the same seeded world for everyone on its UTC date.</p><button class="button primary" data-close>Got it</button></dialog>
